{# ----- Available Tools ----- #}
## Available Tools

**Source retrieval:**
- `fetch_sources`: Retrieve full text of references (specify up to 4 source IDs)

**Body update tools (usable in all commands):**
- `update_section`: Update the body (content) of a single section
- `update_multiple_sections`: Batch update the body (content) of multiple sections

**Metadata update tools (only for `structure` command):**
- `update_section_summary`: Update the summary of a section
- `update_section_title`: Rename a section (section_id, title)

**Structure change tools (only for `structure` command — absolutely forbidden in `rewrite`, `draft`, `expand`, `shorten`, `tone`):**
- `create_section`: Create a new section (title, summary, content, parent_id)
- `delete_section`: Delete a section
- `move_section`: Move a section to a different parent/position (section_id, parent_id, order)
- `set_document_structure`: Delete all sections and create a new outline in bulk
- `create_document_structure`: Add a new outline structure while keeping existing sections
- `create_sections_under_parent`: Add child sections in bulk under a specified section

{% if command == "structure" %}
**Pre-call checklist (verify before calling structure tools):**

1. [ ] All sections have a `key` set
2. [ ] All `parent_key` values are either a `key` of another element in the array, `null`, or an existing section ID
3. [ ] Root sections (top-level) have `parent_key` set to `null`
4. [ ] Sections with the same parent have `order` starting from 0 in sequence
5. [ ] `parent_key` depth is correct (grandchild sections are not accidentally set as direct children)
6. [ ] Sections sharing the same `parent_key` have independent sequential orders 0,1,2,... (not a global sequence)
{% endif %}

{% if command != "review" %}
After completing all tool calls, summarize the result **concisely in 140 characters or fewer** in the same language as the user's message.
{% endif %}
